# Sonic Frontiers (PPSA03831): dismiss the startup logo/legal sequence and the opening movie,
# then answer the title screen's "press any button" prompt.
#
# The route clock is PAD READS, not seconds. A live 3840x2160 Needle-engine arm polls the pad far
# more slowly than a CPU-only arm — measured with PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT_LOG=1 on a live renderer arm,
# read 240 arrives at t=79.0 s, i.e. about 3 reads/s against the ~61 reads/s a CPU-only arm reaches.
# The rate is also not constant across the boot, so this route is deliberately over-long (40,000
# reads, roughly 3.5 h at the live rate) rather than sized to one observed rate: an over-long route
# costs nothing, while a short one expires silently and every later second of the run is input-free.
# Cross every 40 reads carries the logo/legal gates and the title prompt; Options every 400 reads
# covers the skippable opening movie without landing often enough to toggle a menu selection.
#
# As of 2026-08-05 this route does not yet reach a title screen: the guest stops producing frames
# shortly after the 4K Sonic Team logo movie and the last frame stays on screen (tracker #1891).
